From ac48d2549a6307f601528e2ad2ae292d665288e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r8s <r8s@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:15:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] r8s: GPU (G3D) clock over ACPM DVFS + opt-in panfrost devfreq

CMU_G3D belongs to the ACPM firmware. The Samsung 4.19 kernel sets the GPU
clock only via cal_dfs_set_rate(0x0B04000A) -> exynos_acpm_set_rate(10),
in kHz, with no regulator call: ACPM applies the ASV voltage itself, as
for the CPU clusters.

Replace the 800 MHz fixed-clock stub with a clk provider (child of the
ACPM node) that maps rates to ACPM DVFS id 10 on channel 5:
- no ACPM traffic at probe; rate reads as 0 until something sets it;
- set_rate is refused (-EPERM) unless booted with r8s_gpu_dvfs=1, and
  refused (-EAGAIN) while pd_g3d reports off, as Samsung's driver does;
- only the 7 levels Samsung uses (156..800 MHz) are accepted;
- debugfs exynos990-g3d/status reads ACPM get_rate(10) on demand;
  exynos990-g3d/set_khz exists only with r8s_gpu_dvfs=1.

Add the OPP table (377 MHz as opp-suspend, mirroring Samsung's 9830
wakeup-clock workaround), #cooling-cells and a gpu-thermal cooling map.
panfrost devfreq stays off unless loaded with r8s_devfreq=1.

Not tested on the device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
